WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.300
-Nice to see you at number one.
Not too shabby, buddy.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.434
-You know...
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:08.534
-Can I say before we start --
So, every time I come here,

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:11.367
Jimmy puts a kind of gift basket
in my room,

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.567
and it's always so sweet
and thought out.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:14.868
It's giving me a vinyl.

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:16.434
It's, like, a letter
to my daughter and stuff.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.501
I just want to say
it's really nice. Really nice.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:21.634
-Aw. Geez. Thank you.
Thank you, man. Please.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:24.434
I thought you were gonna
make fun of what I gave you.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:27.033
By the way,
I just want to tell you

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:29.300
that your daughter is just
the most beautiful thing.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.701
-Thank you.
-Congratulations on being a dad.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:33.133
This is the first time
on the show as a dad.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:36.868
Congratulations,
you and your wife. Lyra.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:40.033
-She's back -- She's backstage.
-First time on "Fallon."

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.834
-She's the cutest baby.
-[ Audience awws ]

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.767
-And me and my wife
had our second date the night --

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.934
I did "Fallon" in 20--
I say "Fallon."

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.234
I did "Jimmy" in 2015.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.033
And we went out
for our second date that night,

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.367
and we just were, like,
reminiscing backstage there.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:54.934
-Isn't that great?
-Really cool.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.033
-I love that. Good.
There's good vibes here.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.801
She's one.
-She's one, yeah.

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:01.467
-Did she say "Jimmy" yet
or anything?

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:04.734
-No, she does --

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.667
She says, "Dada,"
and points at me.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.667
So I'm now like,
"Okay, now she knows."

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.434
But before,
she'd just say, "Dada,"

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:12.501
and, like, point at an orange
or something.

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.100
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.
Why not? Yeah.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.200
Do you play --- Obviously,
you play music for her.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.067
But do you play the classics?

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:21.567
Do you a big, oh, "Baby Shark"?
Do-do-do-do-do-do?

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.834
-We haven't quite got
to "Baby Shark" yet,

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:25.501
but, no, it's --

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:27.234
Very good, by the way.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:30.000
-What, "Baby Shark"?
Do-do-do-do-do-do?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.167
-Yeah.
Why don't you sing it, though?

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.300
Do you not want to --

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.567
-My voice hurts.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.968
I feel you. I feel you.

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:37.934
-Dude, let's talk about this,
by the way.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.167
Another number-one album.
I mean...

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.200
You cold? Whew.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.100
-I just --
-Wow. You're excited.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.601
Are you cold?

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:49.367
-I just feel the buzz
of number one.

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:51.133
-Yeah, you feel the buzz. Yeah.
-It's in me. It's in me.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:53.267
-Number one.
Number one, everyone.

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:56.133
I want to say this. Over
a billion streams on Spotify.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.334
A billion.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.234
-You know,
I read something about you

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.234
that I thought was cool.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.334
I don't know it was "Shivers"
or what was --

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.100
What was the first single
off this one?

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.801
-"Bad Habits."
-So "Bad Habits" was on, yeah.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.601
-Just sending the vibe, Jimmy.
-Yeah, I saw you.

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.567
But then "Shivers"
is coming out.

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:15.100
"Bad Habits" went to number one.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.834
"Shivers" coming out,
knocking you --

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:19.300
yourself out of number one
with your other song.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.634
It's like -- Yeah.
And then your buddy

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:23.834
Elton John comes out
with a song with Dua Lipa.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.734
And here's the thing that --
Earmuffs.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:28.367
Maybe just plug your ears.
Ed's so cool.

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.434
He goes through everyone on --
and all his fans and goes,

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:32.868
"Hey. Elton's gonna hit
number one.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.767
He's a good friend of mine.
I want him to hit number one.

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:38.133
So go stream his song,
'Cold Heart.'"

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:41.868
-So, can I interject that?
So the reason --

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.667
-Was I close? Was I close?

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:47.934
-But basically --
So, he had started --

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.234
When I had my daughter,
he started ringing me

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:53.167
once a week to just check up
on me being a new dad.

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:55.167
And then I had a friend
that passed away,

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:57.467
and then he started ringing me
every day to check up on me.

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.200
So we speak --
I spoke to him this morning.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.467
I spoke to him yesterday.

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:01.734
I'll speak to him
tomorrow morning.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.133
We speak every day.
And when his song came out,

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.801
he was so buzzed
about being top 20.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.868
And he was like,
"I'm 74, and I'm top 20."

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.934
And then it went top ten,
and then it went top five,

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:10.968
and it was climbing up,
and it was the week

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:14.667
where it was gonna go
number one, and I just like --

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.934
I would feel like a weird guy
if I was speaking to him

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:19.033
the whole time being like,
"Man, I'm so happy for you,"

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:21.267
but then at the last moment
be like, "[Bleep] you."

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.167
-[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.367
-"Yeah. I'm getting
the number one." Yeah.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.067
"We're friends, but -- Yeah."
-I want -- Yeah.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:30.501
And we've got a Christmas song
coming out together.

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:33.534
-Wait. You and Elton John?
-Me and Elton John. Yeah.

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:35.467
-He's got one of my favorite
Christmas songs ever.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:38.033
-Yeah, well, so he --
-"Step into Christmas"?

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:41.501
-Yeah, so, he rung me
on Christmas Day and said --

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:43.767
'Cause he was so buzzed that --
"Step into Christmas"

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:45.801
gets a higher chart position
every single year.

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:47.868
So I think it went in at 13
in the '80s,

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:50.267
and it was like number 6
last year in England.

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.934
So he's like, "I want to do
another Christmas song.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.133
Do you want to do one with me?"

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:54.367
And I've always been
quite against --

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.267
Not that I don't like Christmas.
I love Christmas.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.400
But in terms of doing
a Christmas song,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.868
you need to chuck
the kitchen sink at it.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:01.767
If you're going to do it --
-Got to be able to do it.

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.267
-I have a Northern Irish friend
that says,

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.834
"If you're gonna get done
for stealing a horse,

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:06.200
you might as well [bleep] it."
You know?

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.534
[ Rim shot ]

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:14.334
-Stealing the horse?
-Yeah.

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:17.067
So I said to Elton. I was like,
"I don't really want

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.167
to do a Christmas song
unless we're going in.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:23.033
Unless it's like -- Unless it's
like sleigh bells, ding-dong.

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:25.801
Yeah, it needs to be
a proper Christmas song."

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:29.033
So I wrote a chorus, and then
I went to go and stay with him.

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.534
And we wrote three,
and one of them

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.133
was this one called
"Merry Christmas."

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.267
Okay. So get this.
So, we write it.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.300
And I title it
"Merry Christmas."

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.234
And I'm like, "We're gonna
have to change that title

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.567
'cause there's probably loads of
songs called 'Merry Christmas.'"

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.968
I went on Spotify, and
I typed in "Merry Christmas."

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.767
Nothing. There's "Merry
Christmas, Everyone."

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:48.367
There's "Happy Xmas,"
"Merry Xmas," "War is Over."

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:50.133
There's not a song
called "Merry Christmas."

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:51.601
And then I went on YouTube
and checked it out.

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:53.167
And it baffled me.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:56.267
Like, there's -- It's kind of
like this glitch in a video game

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:58.167
where no one thought...
-Wow!

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.901
-No one thought to -- Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:03.334
'Cause my new horse --
"My new horse." Sorry.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:07.868
♪♪

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:10.067
Congrats on that song.
Congrats on everything.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.868
You got to come back
more often, buddy.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.934
I miss you, and I love
having you on the show.

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:15.601
Ed Sheeran, everybody.
-Thank you.

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:17.300
-"Equals" is out now.

